OrcheRoute for Debian and Astra Linux
=====================================

Install the downloaded package through APT so recommended routing components
are resolved automatically:

  sudo apt install ./OrcheRoute-Linux-Server-VERSION-amd64.deb

Direct `dpkg -i` installation still starts the WebUI. If nftables or iptables
is absent, install them before enabling VPN routing or the inbound AWG server:

  sudo apt install nftables iptables

The package installs the unified Go implementation and does not overwrite or
remove host-specific configuration and state:

  /etc/orcheroute/runtime.env
  /etc/orcheroute/config.json
  /var/lib/orcheroute/network-active.json
  /var/lib/orcheroute/

The control plane and update timers start during installation. On an already
configured host, routing and Mihomo also restart. On a clean host, the VPN
transport waits for the first explicit Enable command in WebUI.

WebUI listeners are configured by orcheroute-go.service. The default server
ports are HTTP 19110 and HTTPS 19111.

The installer prints all local/LAN HTTP addresses and the Basic-auth login.
Initial credentials are also stored root-only in:

  /etc/orcheroute/initial-credentials

`apt remove orcheroute` keeps configuration, credentials, subscriptions,
routes, state and backups for a future reinstall. `apt purge orcheroute`
removes all OrcheRoute configuration, state and backups.
